WHO   — Kshatriya — the arms · warriors & rulers
WHAT  — The class of kings, warriors, and administrators — prowess, protection, governance. The arms that hold the weapon and the throne, ranked second below the priestly mouth.
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because power needed a sacred place in the order too — the sword and the crown, blessed but below the priest.
HOW   — By martial prowess, rule, and the protection of the realm and its dharma.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I hold the sword and the throne — and still the hymn puts the mouth above the arm, the blessing above the blade.

